WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.566
"What are you talking about, Maggie?" Cole asked.

2
00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.787
"Why would Mr. Tate steal his own flavor?"

3
00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:24.339
"I see what Maggie's saying," Henry said.

4
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:29.766
"What if bubble gum banana swirl isn't really Mr. Tate's invention?

5
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.319
What if Mrs. Sweet came up with it first?"

6
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:39.509
"Mr. Tate could be trying to frame Mrs. Sweet by saying she stole it from him," Maggie said.

7
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.201
"He claims she doesn't want competition from the Dessert Den.

8
00:00:43.202 --> 00:00:46.947
But maybe he's the one who's trying to steal customers!"

9
00:00:46.948 --> 00:00:50.725
Cole shrugged. "I guess that's a pretty good motive.

10
00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:53.568
But we just talked to Mrs. Sweet.

11
00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:57.785
Wouldn't she have told us that bubble gum banana swirl is her flavor?"

12
00:00:57.786 --> 00:01:01.301
"She's really nice," Maggie reminded them.

13
00:01:01.302 --> 00:01:04.268
"Maybe she didn't want to get Mr. Tate in trouble.

14
00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:07.252
Even if he is a dirty flavor thief!"

15
00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:11.449
"I guess we should check out your idea, Maggie," Henry said.

16
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:17.271
"Like I said, good detectives follow up on every lead and theory."

17
00:01:17.272 --> 00:01:19.659
Then he thought of another question.

18
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:28.815
"But if Mrs. Sweet invented bubble gum banana swirl, why didn't she tell Patty how she came up with the flavor?"

19
00:01:28.816 --> 00:01:31.235
"Good question," Cole said.

20
00:01:31.236 --> 00:01:34.391
"Usually she has a story to go along with all her flavors.

21
00:01:34.392 --> 00:01:37.370
Like raspberry mint chip, for instance."

22
00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:39.228
Maggie grabbed her bike.

23
00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:44.114
"Just because Patty didn't know the story doesn't mean there isn't one," she said.

24
00:01:44.115 --> 00:01:47.530
"Let's go back to the Sweet Shop and ask Mrs. Sweet!"

25
00:01:47.531 --> 00:01:52.968
She raced off down the sidewalk. Henry and Cole followed.

26
00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:58.975
As they rounded the corner, Henry saw Robby and some other kids sitting on the grass, drinking sodas.

27
00:01:58.976 --> 00:02:02.021
"Wait!" he called to his friends.

28
00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:06.339
He wanted to stop and ask Robby why he was so mad at Mr. Tate.

29
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:11.845
Plus, maybe one of the West Belltown kids had seen Mr. Tate do something suspicious.

30
00:02:11.846 --> 00:02:15.071
But Maggie and Cole were too far ahead to hear him.

31
00:02:15.072 --> 00:02:19.770
Henry shrugged and kept going. He waved at Robby as he passed him.

32
00:02:19.771 --> 00:02:25.555
But Robby just stared back at him.

33
00:02:25.556 --> 00:02:29.954
When they neared the Sweet Shop, Henry saw Mr. Moss standing outside.

34
00:02:29.955 --> 00:02:34.502
He was painting the shop's window frame.

35
00:02:34.503 --> 00:02:37.790
"Hello, kids," Mr. Moss said cheerfully.

36
00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:40.293
"Are you here to get some ice cream?"

37
00:02:40.294 --> 00:02:44.524
"Actually, we came to talk to Mrs. Sweet," Maggie said.

38
00:02:44.525 --> 00:02:46.414
"I haven't seen her yet.

39
00:02:46.415 --> 00:02:50.389
I just got here a few minutes ago myself," Mr. Moss said.

40
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.845
"I wanted to surprise her by getting started on this painting she asked me to do."

41
00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:59.480
He held up his paintbrush and smiled. "She might be inside."

42
00:02:59.481 --> 00:03:05.212
The kids left their bikes leaning against the lamppost and entered the Sweet Shop.

43
00:03:05.213 --> 00:03:07.691
Patty was still behind the counter.

44
00:03:07.692 --> 00:03:12.310
"Hi. Is Mrs. Sweet around?" Henry asked her.

45
00:03:12.311 --> 00:03:16.501
"Sorry, no. She left half an hour ago to run an errand."

46
00:03:16.502 --> 00:03:21.551
Henry was disappointed. They really needed to talk to Mrs. Sweet!

47
00:03:21.552 --> 00:03:25.584
"We were wondering about something," he said to Patty.

48
00:03:25.585 --> 00:03:29.774
"How long has bubble gum banana swirl been on the menu?"

49
00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:34.096
"Hmm, let me think." Patty tapped her chin.

50
00:03:34.097 --> 00:03:37.074
"I remember serving it on Monday afternoon.

51
00:03:37.075 --> 00:03:39.850
Mrs. Sweet must have added it that morning."

52
00:03:39.851 --> 00:03:44.128
"Monday?" Henry traded a look with his friends.

53
00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:47.872
"Do you kids want to order anything?" Patty glanced outside.

54
00:03:47.873 --> 00:03:50.240
"If so, you should probably do it now.

55
00:03:50.241 --> 00:03:53.636
It looks like a whole crowd of customers just arrived."

56
00:03:53.637 --> 00:03:56.123
Henry looked out the front window.

57
00:03:56.124 --> 00:03:59.314
A van had just stopped by the curb outside.

58
00:03:59.315 --> 00:04:02.920
A bunch of little kids were jumping out of it.

59
00:04:02.921 --> 00:04:05.791
"No, thanks," he told Patty.

60
00:04:05.792 --> 00:04:09.368
The little kids rushed in, along with a couple of adults.

61
00:04:09.369 --> 00:04:15.963
As they clustered around the counter, Henry and his friends moved over to a private corner.

62
00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:20.469
"Now we know how long Mrs. Sweet has had that flavor," Cole said.

63
00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:25.245
"But we don't know when Mr. Tate invented it," Henry said.

64
00:04:25.246 --> 00:04:28.508
"We need to find out when he painted his sign.

65
00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:33.067
If it was after Monday morning, he's probably guilty.

66
00:04:33.068 --> 00:04:37.166
But if it was before Monday, then he's innocent."

67
00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:42.441
"He's guilty." Maggie sounded confident. "Let's go ask him."

68
00:04:42.442 --> 00:04:44.023
"Do you think he'll tell us the truth?"

69
00:04:44.024 --> 00:04:46.963
Cole wondered as they headed toward the door.

70
00:04:46.964 --> 00:04:50.866
They had to stop a few times to dodge excited little kids.

71
00:04:50.867 --> 00:04:52.536
Maggie shrugged.

72
00:04:52.537 --> 00:04:59.641
"Why wouldn't he tell us the truth? He thinks we're on his side, remember?"

73
00:04:59.642 --> 00:05:05.121
Outside the Sweet Shop, nobody was around. Even Mr. Moss had disappeared.

74
00:05:05.122 --> 00:05:12.331
Cole looked around in confusion. "Hey," he said. "Where are our bikes?"

75
00:05:12.332 --> 00:05:18.018
Just then Mr. Moss hurried into view from the alley between the Sweet Shop and the building next door.

76
00:05:18.019 --> 00:05:20.662
He was holding a new can of paint.

77
00:05:20.663 --> 00:05:25.279
"Hello again, kids," he said. "Did you find Mrs. Sweet?"

78
00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:30.054
"No," said Maggie. "And now someone stole our bikes!"

79
00:05:30.055 --> 00:05:35.097
"Wait!" Cole called. "I see them! Look—over there!"

80
00:05:35.098 --> 00:05:38.388
Henry looked where Cole was pointing and gasped.

81
00:05:38.389 --> 00:05:43.457
Their bikes were lying in a jumbled pile behind the van!
